NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000261 "patch to an existing test-file that illustrates the bug or desired"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000262 "feature."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000263 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000264 "=head1 SEE ALSO"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000265 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000266 "L<Data::Rmap>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000267 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000268 "L<Data::Visitor::Callback>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000269 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000270 "L<Data::Abridge> is similar in goal, which is to let Perl data structures (which"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000271 "might contain stuffs unsupported in JSON) be encodeable to JSON. But unlike"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000272 "Data::Clean::JSON, it has some (currently) non-configurable rules, like changing"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000273 "a coderef with a hash C<< {CODE=>'\\&main::__ANON__'} >> or a scalar ref with C<<"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000274 "{SCALAR=>'value'} >> and so on. Note that the abridging process is similarly"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000275 "unidirectional (you cannot convert back the original Perl data structure)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000276 ""
